20592.0 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap declared=57 visible=56 resolved=57 missing=0 first=NATURE/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS008 resource=materials/Nature/dirtground001_height-ssbump.vtf reason=the materials name 31 distinct $bumpmap textures, so the one sampler slot the pass started with cannot apply each material's own; per-material binding is the --world-material-bump switch, and with it on the 16 that do not set $ssbump sample their own tile through a texinfo-axis tangent basis while the 41 that do stay refused (see the $ssbump row)
20592.0 gpu: world feature feature=bumpmap2 declared=1 visible=1 resolved=1 missing=0 first=COALMINES/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS_COALMINES resource=materials/Nature/dirtground003_height-ssbump.vtf reason=$bumpmap2 is layer 2's normal map: it is lerped into layer 1's normal by the vertex blend weight, so it is sampled only when --world-material-bump and --world-bump2 are both on; with either off it is refused, not silently replaced by layer 1's; 1/1 of those materials also declare $ssbump, so their second-layer texel is a bumpBasis weight and stays refused even with both switches on (--world-bump2-texture measures the layer with a diagnostic normal map instead)
20592.0 gpu: world feature feature=ssbump declared=41 visible=41 resolved=41 missing=0 first=NATURE/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS008 resource=Nature/dirtground001_height-ssbump reason=$ssbump selects `BUMPMAP == 2`, where the texel is not a signed normal but three bumpBasis weights against three lightmap directions; this pass samples one lightmap and one tangent-space normal, so these materials are refused by name even when --world-material-bump is on
20592.0 gpu: world feature feature=detail declared=53 visible=51 resolved=0 missing=53 first=WOOD/WOOD_BEAM02 resource=materials/overlays/detail006.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused
